<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Abyss_Rename.xml            mandrake.rm.abyss (ships in mandrake.rm.biomes)

       Moved here from RimUtinni/UtinniPatches 2026-10-03 (ABYSS_FREE_TIER_BODY_1 step 1):
       the invented labels are not IP (Q11a), so the free tier shows them too;
       the campaign still gets them because it loads this mod.

       NONCANON_BEAST_RENAME_1 batch 3a — Abyss. Owner ruled batch 3
       applied 2026-09-24 (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
       noncanon_beast_names_crags_nightside_contagion_slime.md). Fourteen donor
       ThingDef+PawnKindDef pairs (13 Alpha Animals AA_, 1 Vanilla Genetics
       Expanded GR_) get a label/description patch, following the
       PatchOperationConditional gate pattern of RotSpecies_NamesAndSizes.xml:
       each block is gated on the ThingDef's own xpath existing, so an absent
       donor mod makes the block no-op silently — no MayRequire needed.

       LABEL ONLY on the identity; no defName, stat, or art field is touched.

       ABYSS_SHEET_DONOR_PORT_1 (2026-10-06): the blocks for the eight donors ported to owned
       RM_ defs (AA_Nightling, AA_NightRam, AA_NightMule, AA_CrepuscularBeetle,
       AA_DarkVandal, AA_DuskProwler, AA_Darkbeast) are deleted; the owner's sheet superseded
       those labels and the Abyss no longer casts the donors. AA_Murkling's block is KEPT:
       the Abyss casts its port RM_Lirrith instead, but the donor itself still ships in
       RUT_CrackedLands and RM_FloodedCanyon (WildAnimals_CrackedLands.xml), which keep
       showing it as "kessik".
       Not drafted here: AA_DuskRat (owner ruled the name IS the joke, kept),
       AA_SandProwler (already port-named RSW_Vosska "vosska"). -->

  <!-- ============== AA_Murkling -> kessik ============== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Murkling"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Murkling"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>kessik</label></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Murkling"]/description</xpath>
          <value><description>A small, quick-witted scavenger that runs in packs, humming to its kin through organs on its snout that no other ear can follow. Sly enough to outwit prey twice its size, the kessik has a reputation across the crags as the thief of the night — and a bite that leaves more than a scar behind.</description></value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="AA_Murkling"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="AA_Murkling"]/label</xpath>
      <value><label>kessik</label></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>


